  "worked_solution": "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1-2x} & =5 \\\\ ln\u2061({e}^{1-2x}) & =ln\u2061(5) \\\\ 1-2x & =ln\u2061(5) \\\\ -2x & =ln\u2061(5)-1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1-ln\u2061(5)}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\u2248-0.305\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
